  "notes": "{数|かぞ}える is an ichidan verb meaning 'to count' or 'to enumerate.'\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{数|かぞ}える\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {数|かぞ}え⟦{切|き}れない→切れる：01936_kireru⟧: countless, too many to count\n- ⟦{指折|ゆびお}り→指折り：18050_yubiori⟧{数|かぞ}える: count on fingers (eagerly await)\n- ⟦{日|ひ}→日：02249_hi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{数|かぞ}える: count the days\n- ⟦{人数|にんずう}→人数：03132_ninzuu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{数|かぞ}える: count the number of people\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{数|かず}→数：00204_kazu⟧: number (noun)\n- ⟦{数字|すうじ}→数字：03361_suuji⟧: numeral, digit\n- ⟦{計算|けいさん}する→計算する：25526_keisansuru⟧: to calculate\n\nUSAGE:\nThe kanji 数 appears in both the noun ⟦{数|かず}→数：00204_kazu⟧ (number) and the verb {数|かぞ}える (to count).",
